id:                     E339
trigger_tool:           g_test|GDBusServer|GDBusConnection|unix socket|authentication worker
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        gdbus.*TIMEOUT|authentication.*timeout|worker.*wait|480.*seconds
severity:               2
category:               testing, portability, runtime-capability, ipc
match_keywords:         constructor probe, Unix address form, authentication handshake, trap subprocess, worker timeout
title:                  Probe IPC constructors before isolating blocking authentication tests

root_cause:             A successful socket bind does not prove that the library constructor can create every address form or that the authentication worker will make progress. Entering a blocking peer vector after only a low-level bind can leave the whole test binary waiting until the CI harness timeout.
affected_scope:         Cross-platform IPC test suites that construct Unix-domain or equivalent authenticated streams on restricted kernels and sandboxes.
verification_cmd:       Run each affected test binary with the normal harness; probe each constructor address form without worker threads, then run the vector in an exec'ed child with a finite timeout and preserve unexpected failures.

rec_priority:            1
rec_approach:            constructor-before-worker
rec_description:        Perform a no-worker constructor probe for every address spelling used by the test. Cache only an explicitly classified capability-unavailable result. Put the full blocking vector behind g_test_trap_subprocess() so an optional handshake timeout becomes a local skip rather than a global CI timeout.
rec_command:             meson test -C build --print-errorlogs gio:gdbus-peer gio:gdbus-server-auth gio:gdbus-connection-flush
rec_auto_fix:            false
rec_impl:                gdbus-constructor-probe-and-bounded-vector

fallback_priority:       2
fallback_approach:       fail-closed-on-unknown
fallback_description:    If constructor creation returns an unclassified error or a child exits unexpectedly, keep the test failing. Do not broaden capability markers or treat a timeout as proof that all transports are unsupported.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:       false
fallback_impl:           explicit-capability-classification

forbid_1_pattern:        g_test_trap_fork.*GDBusServer|bind.*success.*authentication
forbid_1_reason:         Forking a worker-bearing GDBus probe can inherit the same deadlock, while bind success alone misses constructor and authentication failures.
forbid_1_consequence:    CI consumes the complete harness timeout and reports an environmental failure without a bounded test result.
forbid_2_pattern:        timeout.*increase|skip.*all.*gdbus|ignore.*authentication
forbid_2_reason:         Global skips and larger deadlines hide real regressions and remove unrelated IPC coverage.
forbid_2_consequence:    The suite loses signal and still risks indefinite waits on the next blocking path.

principles:              P002, P006, P014
causes:                  []
caused_by:               []
similar_to:              []
conflicts_with:          []
prerequisite_of:         []

